/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132858794,imgsize-1069850.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Biodiversity boosts forest growth; loss could cut gains 17% by 2050]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132858357.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-tracked-global-forest-photosynthesis-for-20-years-and-found-species-rich-forests-improved-faster-biodiversity-loss-could-reduce-the-trend-by-up-to-17-by-2050/articleshow/132858357.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-tracked-global-forest-photosynthesis-for-20-years-and-found-species-rich-forests-improved-faster-biodiversity-loss-could-reduce-the-trend-by-up-to-17-by-2050/articleshow/132858357.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T16:32:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132858524,imgsize-398129.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[World's oldest amber has been found in China, and it is 65 million years older than expected]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132851769.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a remarkable discovery, scientists uncovered ancient amber specimens in China that are approximately 385 million years old. This significant find pushes the amber fossil record back by an impressive sixty-five million years. It indicates that early vascular plants may have developed advanced resin-producing capabilities, which could have provided a defensive advantage against wildfires and fungal diseases. The research advances our understanding of plant resilience during the Devonian era.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/worlds-oldest-amber-has-been-found-in-china-and-it-is-65-million-years-older-than-expected/articleshow/132851769.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/worlds-oldest-amber-has-been-found-in-china-and-it-is-65-million-years-older-than-expected/articleshow/132851769.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T14:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132851769,imgsize-204059.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Long before GPS, Polynesian sailors crossed the Pacific by reading stars, waves, winds, birds and clouds]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132851511.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/long-before-gps-polynesian-sailors-crossed-the-pacific-by-reading-stars-waves-winds-birds-and-clouds/articleshow/132851511.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/long-before-gps-polynesian-sailors-crossed-the-pacific-by-reading-stars-waves-winds-birds-and-clouds/articleshow/132851511.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T13:45:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132851628,imgsize-1321195.cms"/></item></channel></rss>